Bonjour! Here's an example of a SwiftUI view that displays a list of menu items, loads images asynchronously using `AsyncImage`, and includes a pull-to-refresh functionality using `refreshable`.

### ✅ Features:
- Async image loading using `AsyncImage`.
- Pull-to-refresh with `refreshable`.
- Sample data using a `MenuItem` struct.

---

### 📦 Example SwiftUI View

```swift
import SwiftUI

// Sample model
struct MenuItem: Identifiable {
    let id = UUID()
    let name: String
    let price: String
    let imageUrl: String
}

// Sample data
let sampleMenuItems = [
    MenuItem(name: "Burger", price: "$10.99", imageUrl: "https://example.com/burger.jpg"),
    MenuItem(name: "Pasta", price: "$12.99", imageUrl: "https://example.com/pasta.jpg"),
    MenuItem(name: "Salad", price: "$8.99", imageUrl: "https://example.com/salad.jpg")
]

struct MenuView: View {
    @State private var menuItems: [MenuItem] = sampleMenuItems
    @State private var isRefreshing = false

    var body: some View {
        NavigationView {
            List {
                ForEach(menuItems) { item in
                    HStack {
                        AsyncImage(url: URL(string: item.imageUrl)) { image in
                            image
                                .resizable()
                                .scaledToFill()
                                .frame(width: 60, height: 60)
                                .cornerRadius(8)
                        } placeholder: {
                            Color.gray
                                .frame(width: 60, height: 60)
                                .cornerRadius(8)
                        }

                        VStack(alignment: .leading) {
                            Text(item.name)
                                .font(.headline)
                            Text(item.price)
                                .foregroundColor(.secondary)
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            .navigationTitle("Menu")
            .refreshable {
                isRefreshing = true
                await refreshMenu()
            }
        }
    }

    func refreshMenu() async {
        // Simulate network delay
        try? await Task.sleep(nanoseconds: 2_000_000_000)

        // In a real app, you would fetch new data from an API here
        menuItems = sampleMenuItems.shuffled()

        isRefreshing = false
    }
}
```

---

### 📌 Notes:
- `AsyncImage` is used to load images asynchronously and efficiently.
- The `refreshable` modifier handles pull-to-refresh logic.
- The `refreshMenu()` function simulates a network call and updates the list with new (or shuffled) data.

---

